    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161-a6">

                <pb facs="0570" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg356"/>

                <head>Mr. Washburne to Archbishop Chigi</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>
                            11, 1871. </date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Colleague:</hi> Mr. McKean, my private
                    secretary, will call on you in relation to the archbishop. He will hand you a
                    copy of a memorandum made by him on the subject of an exchange for Blanqui. I
                    need not assure you that I shall be very glad to do anything that is proper in
                    this Shatter—officiously, of course—to facilitate any arrangement that might be
                    made. Mr. McKean visited the archbishop with me yesterday, and can explain to
                    you fully in regard to him.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
